GLM-5.3-Flash-FP4-Local TensorFold Dual Spark recipe

This recipe adds a TensorFold storage reader for NVIDIA's FP4-Local mixed
checkpoint, lossless CSF32 expert-scale expansion, fused compatible dense
projections, a proposal-only Q4 head and decode/prefill work counters. It also
adds verified repeated-span copy proposals and cached-request scheduling
changes to TensorFold's existing prompt-lookup and batched serving paths.

The patches modify TensorFold and the MiaAI-Lab GLM Spark runtime. Their
copyright, Apache-2.0 and earlier MIT notices are retained in
third_party/MiaAI-NOTICE.txt and third_party/Apache-2.0.txt. The original
runtime credits are preserved in third_party/MiaAI-CREDITS.md. The thirteen
Bespoke patches are backports from the MiaAI-Lab project's pull requests;
their origin and commit identifiers are recorded in provenance.json.

The CSF32 decoder follows the lossless scale-plane layout implemented by
FlashInfer/b12x (Apache-2.0):
https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer/tree/main/flashinfer/experimental/b12x
The GPU NVFP4, MXFP8 and FP8 kernels are TensorFold's existing kernels.

The TensorFold logo used as the cover reference belongs to the TensorFold
project. The cover depicts this independent recipe and implies no vendor
or upstream endorsement.

Model weights and container binaries are not included. NVIDIA's target
checkpoint uses the NVIDIA Open Model Agreement. IncoAI's DFlash2 checkpoint
uses CC BY-NC-ND 4.0; the measured speculative configuration is non-commercial.
The pinned base container retains its NVIDIA and third-party software terms.

No new project-wide license has been assigned to the owner's original
recipe files. Third-party code and notices retain their applicable terms.
